  "method": "SoQL count of complaints grouped by year of RPT_DT (report date) and offense key code. Offense mapping (KY_CD = OFNS_DESC): 101 = MURDER & NON-NEGL. MANSLAUGHTER; 104 = RAPE; 105 = ROBBERY; 106 = FELONY ASSAULT; 107 = BURGLARY; 109 = GRAND LARCENY; 110 = GRAND LARCENY OF MOTOR VEHICLE. The script checks that each code carries exactly that description (a few rows carry the code with a blank description; they are counted by code). All rows in these codes are felonies (LAW_CAT_CD = FELONY). Historic file through December 31, 2025; the year-to-date file starts January 1, 2026, so there is no overlap.",
  "caveats": [
    "Totals from complaint data can differ slightly from NYPD CompStat figures, which are compiled separately.",
    "New York State broadened its legal definition of rape effective September 2024, which affects comparisons of the rape component (complaints: 1,452 in 2023, 1,749 in 2024, 2,049 in 2025).",
    "Peers: crime categories and counting rules differ across police departments (the FBI uses its own definitions, and the NYPD's seven majors are a local grouping), so no peer comparison is given.",
    "8 2025 complaints had no borough recorded.",
